# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Read by scripts/deploy-sepolia.sh.
#
# Anything already set in your environment wins over this file, so an inline
# `RPC_URL=... bun run deploy:sepolia` still overrides what is here.
#
# Every variable the deploy reads is listed below. Commented lines show the built-in default, so
# this file doubles as the reference for what those defaults are.

# ─── Required ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Deployer key. Use a throwaway — the deploy broadcasts real transactions, and this file exists so
# the key stays out of your shell history, not because it is safe to reuse a real one.
PRIVATE_KEY=

# ─── Optional: network ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# A public endpoint is the default. Swap in Alchemy/Infura if you hit rate limits — the deploy makes
# a lot of calls in a short window.
# RPC_URL=https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com

# ─── Optional: Sepolia targets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Defaults track the current Interfold Sepolia deployment. Override only if you are pointing at a
# different one — a mismatched Interfold address makes `request` revert with empty data, which is
# close to undiagnosable from the revert alone.
#
# These four move together. A stack redeploy replaces all of them, and mixing addresses from two
# deployments fails in ways that look like contract bugs rather than configuration.

# INTERFOLD_ADDRESS=0xDF46f767b95BF018d4E5FF6Be41Fae437E47AC1C
# CRISP_PROGRAM_ADDRESS=0xD980bB00Ee3dfB6da0110CF65529D074c8934f35
# FEE_TOKEN_ADDRESS=0xA386a424c30F519c7d51Cc809d538AEC3000c17C
# FAUCET_ADDRESS=0x1568D441eCC08998ce81A6B3F2655811F9fAb0C3
# CRISP_SERVER_URL=https://private-crisp.theinterfold.com

# ─── Optional: E3 request shape ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# COMMITTEE_SIZE indexes Interfold's committee thresholds: 0 Minimum, 1 Micro, 2 Small. PARAM_SET
# indexes the registered BFV parameter sets: 0 is the insecure-512 testnet preset.

# COMMITTEE_SIZE=0
# PARAM_SET=0
# COMPUTE_PROVIDER_PARAMS=0x7b226e616d65223a225249534330222c22706172616c6c656c223a66616c73652c2262617463685f73697a65223a347d

# ─── Optional: lobby floors ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These two bound what a lobby may choose in the app. They are the only timing values that outlive
# the deploy — everything in the next section shapes only the dry-run rehearsal, because the deploy
# creates no standalone game.

# The plugin's minimum ballot, in seconds. Permanent: set when the plugin is initialised, and a
# lower bound on every lobby ever created against it. Changing it later means another deploy.
# MIN_DURATION=180

# The app's minimum campaign, in whole minutes. Written into app/.env as
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MIN_CAMPAIGN_MINUTES. The campaign has to outlast committee sortition and the DKG —
# seconds when the ciphernodes skip proof aggregation, minutes when they do not.
# MIN_CAMPAIGN_MINUTES=1

# ─── Optional: rehearsal round shape ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Used by `--dry-run` only. Real lobbies are configured in the app, so these no longer decide what
# anyone plays — they decide what the rehearsal exercises before you deploy for real.
#
# TEAM_COUNT and MIN_MEMBERS_PER_TEAM are both ballot option counts, so both are capped at 10 by the
# CRISP circuit. 10 x 10 is the maximum: 100 players, every ballot still provable.

# TEAM_COUNT=4
# MIN_MEMBERS_PER_TEAM=2      # MEMBERS_PER_TEAM is the old name and is still honoured

# MIN_PLAYERS is the lobby floor: how many must join before anyone may start. Seats above it stay
# open until someone does, and any still empty at that moment stay empty for the whole game.
# Defaults to TEAM_COUNT * MIN_MEMBERS_PER_TEAM — the smallest legal start.
#
# It must exceed MERGE_AT, or the game is post-merge from its first round: tribes dissolve
# immediately and every round is an individual vote, making the team configuration decorative.
# MIN_PLAYERS=8

# MERGE_AT is the survivor count at which tribes dissolve.
# MERGE_AT=6
# FINALISTS=2

# CAMPAIGN_DURATION must outlast committee sortition and the DKG, because the ballot window opens
# the moment it ends. Measure it on your first round rather than trusting this.
# CAMPAIGN_DURATION=900

# BALLOT_DURATION is sized for people, not the committee: each ballot is 45-90s of proof generation
# in the browser, and anyone driving several wallets does it sequentially.
#
# Do not buy ballot time by shortening the campaign. Sortition and the DKG run during the campaign
# window, so cutting it below that floor opens the ballot against a committee key that does not exist
# yet — which costs voting time rather than saving it.
# BALLOT_DURATION=2700

# TALLY_GRACE is a deadline, not a delay. A round settles the moment the committee publishes its
# counts; this is how long the committee has before the round may be abandoned instead.
# TALLY_GRACE=600
# MAX_MISSED_CHECKINS=2

# ENTRY_FEE is the per-player buy-in for the rehearsal game. Lobbies created from the app are free
# to join and funded by their creator, so this is 0 by default and only exists for a game deployed
# directly.
# ENTRY_FEE=0

# ─── Optional: carried into app/.env ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Not read by the deploy itself. It copies these from the existing app/.env so a redeploy does not
# silently drop them — campaign posts fall back to on-chain storage without a JWT, and become
# unreadable without a gateway that will serve them.

# PINATA_JWT=
# PINATA_GATEWAY=https://<your-name>.mypinata.cloud
